# Festival of Embers: "If a card or token would be put into your graveyard from anywhere, exile it instead." Bot1 casts Festival on turn 1, then Blood Artist and
# Lingering Souls on turn 3 (two Spirit tokens). On turn 4 Bot2's Lightning Bolt kills a Spirit: the token is exiled instead of dying, so Blood Artist does not trigger
# (both lives 20), while Bot2's own Bolt goes to Bot2's graveyard. Lingering Souls itself was exiled as it resolved. On turn 5 Bot1 pays {1}{R} to sacrifice the Festival, which is exiled as it leaves (it is a card
# bound for Bot1's graveyard). On turn 6 Bot2's second Bolt kills the other Spirit, which dies normally, and Blood Artist triggers: Bot2 19, Bot1 21.

